{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29863 - PROTEIN:5821",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which (+)-Iridodial lactol may interact with MOVP-3, through a series of target-mediated pathways involving Ataxin-2. Ataxin-2 is a target of multiple compounds, including Ancistrobenomine A and 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside, all of which are linked to MOVP-3. This indicates that (+)-Iridodial lactol may act as a modulator of Ataxin-2, potentially influencing its interaction with MOVP-3. The shared target of Ataxin-2 across different compounds suggests a possible common mechanism of action, possibly involving the regulation of MOVP-3 through Ataxin-2. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Ataxin-2 and MOVP-3 supports the hypothesis that (+)-Iridodial lactol may exert its effects through a pathway involving Ataxin-2, which could be a key mediator in the observed relationship with MOVP-3.",
